message: "If you use these analysis scripts, please cite this software release and the associated research paper."

type: software
title: "Multi-Omics Clustering Differentiates the Total and Intact HIV Reservoirs and Related Host Immune Mechanisms: Analysis Code"

authors:
  - family-names: "Rios-Vazquez"
    given-names: "Victoria"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6270-7175"
    affiliation: "Radboud University Medical Center (Radboudumc)"

version: "1.0.0"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/victoriariosvzz2/Multiomics-Clusters-Reservoir-2000HIV"

abstract: >-
  Analysis code accompanying the study "Multi-Omics Clustering Differentiates
  the Total and Intact HIV Reservoirs and Related Host Immune Mechanisms".
  The repository contains R and Python scripts for multi-omics quality control,
  integrative clustering, machine learning and model interpretation,
  differential expression and pathway enrichment, flow cytometry, and
  ex vivo cytokine analyses in the 2000HIV cohort. Documentation and a
  synthetic-data machine learning demonstration are included. Individual-level
  participant data are not distributed with the repository.

keywords:
  - "HIV reservoir"
  - "2000HIV"
  - "multi-omics"
  - "bioinformatics"
  - "machine learning"
  - "immune profiling"
  - "reproducible research"
